<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lluís Companys</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1882–1940</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lluís Companys was a Catalan lawyer and leader of the Republican Left of Catalonia who became president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/generalitat-de-catalunya">Generalitat of Catalonia</a> in 1934 after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesc-macia">Francesc Macià</a>. In October 1934 he proclaimed a Catalan State within a federal Spanish republic and was imprisoned. Restored in 1936, he led Catalonia during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-civil-war">Spanish Civil War</a>. Handed over by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gestapo">Gestapo</a> in 1940, he was executed by Franco's regime.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lluis-companys.jpg" alt="Lluís Companys" width="320" height="459" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Llu%C3%ADs_Companys_i_Jover_(1-E-6412).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
